# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║ dirmarks — named directories, shared by `c` (shell) and `:C` (nvim)  ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
# One bookmark per line:   name <2+ spaces or tab> path <2+ spaces> note
#   • Paths may use ~ and the $ANCHORS from ~/.config/paths.env, so moving a
#     content root stays a one-line edit there.
#   • The note column is fuzzy-searchable in both pickers — put the words you
#     would actually type to find the directory, not a description.
#   • Comments and blank lines survive `c add` / `c rm`, so group freely.
#   • `c edit` (or `:C edit`) opens this file with column alignment on save.

